  3. Combining or Linking the Library with Other Code.

  The "library" of which you have a copy (or have the right to use)
is called the "Library".  This Library may be combined with programs
that are not covered by this License (called "non-Library programs") to
produce a program containing portions of the Library, and to distribute
that program under the terms of your choice.

  The following sections apply when you link the Library with other
code.  "Linking" means creating a single program containing the
Library, or including portions of the Library in a program that is
not itself a work to which the Library applies.

  a) Combined Works.

  You may convey a "combined work" (a single program containing the
Library plus portions of other programs that use the Library).  A
"combined work" is not itself covered by this License; instead, the
terms of this License apply to the combined work as a whole.  The
combined work is not a derivative of the Library.

  If a portion of the combined work is not covered by this License
(the combined work includes non-Library programs), then the terms of
section 7 of this License apply to the combined work as a whole.
In particular, you may satisfy the requirements of this License for
the combined work by distributing the combined work under the terms
of a license of your choice, provided that you also distribute the
Library in object code form, under the terms of this License, and
you do not limit the recipients of the combined work to those who
receive the object code form.

  b) Conveying the Combined Work.

  When the combined work is distributed, you must cause the entire
combined work to be treated as if it were covered by this License,
except as follows:

    i) The combined work need not contain anything that can be
    extracted from the Library itself, except for the Library's
    interface to the rest of the combined work.

    ii) The combined work as a whole is subject to the requirements
    of section 7 of this License.

    iii) The combined work must include the Library, or a copy of it,
    in the combined work's object code form, or include a reference
    to the Library, or include a pointer to the Library.

    iv) You must cause the combined work to do the following:

      - Maintain notices required by section 7 of this License.

      - Treat the entire combined work as a covered work under this
      License.

      - Ensure that the combined work provides the Library with a
      reference to the Library's interface, rather than including
      the Library's implementation.

      - Ensure that the combined work provides the Library's
      interface to the user, rather than including the Library's
      implementation.

      - Ensure that the combined work provides the Library's
      interface to the user in the same manner as if the user had
      obtained the Library separately.

  c) Distribution of the Combined Work.

  When you distribute the combined work, you must include the source
code for the Library with the combined work, as specified in section 6
of this License, or a reference to the Library.  If the combined work
includes the Library's object code, you must also include the object
code for the Library.

  d) Lgpl Incompatibility.

  If you choose to distribute the combined work under a different
license (such as the GPL), you must also distribute the Library's
source code.  This is because the LGPL requires that the Library's
source code be available for modification.

